### Tags API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for tag management and tag attachments endpoints
### All operations for creating, reading, and managing tags and tag attachments
### Reviewed and verified against implementation

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@tagId = your-tag-uuid-here
@attachmentId = your-attachment-uuid-here
@userId = your-user-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp
### - @tagId: UUID of an existing tag
### - @attachmentId: UUID of an existing tag attachment
### - @userId: UUID of an existing user

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE TAG (WITH BADGE UPLOAD)
### ============================================
### Create a new tag with optional badge image
### Requires user JWT token
### Badge upload is optional - tag can be created without a badge

### STEP 1: Get Upload URL for Badge (Optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/s3/upload-url
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fileName": "tag-badge.png",
  "fileType": "image",
  "filePurpose": "tag"
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "data": {
###     "uploadUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###     "file": {
###       "id": "file-uuid-here",
###       "fileName": "tag-badge.png",
###       "fileType": "image",
###       "filePurpose": "tag",
###       "url": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###       ...
###     },
###     "uploadToken": "token-string-here"
###   }
### }

### STEP 2: Upload Badge to S3 (Optional)
### Use the uploadUrl from Step 1 to upload the actual file
### This is a PUT request to the signed URL (not to our API)
### Note: Replace {{uploadUrl}} with the actual URL from Step 1 response

PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/png

< ./path/to/your/tag-badge.png

### STEP 3: Create Tag with Badge
### After uploading badge to S3, use the fileId, uploadToken, and purpose from Step 1
### IMPORTANT: badgeUrl must be an array, even for single files

POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Web Development",
  "badgeUrl": [
    {
      "fileId": "file-uuid-from-step-1",
      "token": "token-from-step-1",
      "purpose": "tag"
    }
  ]
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Tag created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "tag-uuid",
###     "name": "Web Development",
###     "badgeUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 2. CREATE TAG (WITHOUT BADGE)
### ============================================
### Create a tag without a badge image
### Badge is optional, so you can create tags without uploading any files

POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Graphic Design"
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Tag created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "tag-uuid",
###     "name": "Graphic Design",
###     "badgeUrl": "",
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 3. LIST ALL TAGS
### ============================================
### Get all tags in the system
### No authentication required
### Returns all tags with their badges

GET {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Tags fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "tag-uuid-1",
###       "name": "Web Development",
###       "badgeUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###       "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###     },
###     {
###       "id": "tag-uuid-2",
###       "name": "Graphic Design",
###       "badgeUrl": "",
###       "createdAt": "2024-01-02T00:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2024-01-02T00:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### 4. CREATE TAG ATTACHMENT
### ============================================
### Create a tag attachment (user submits proof/document for a tag)
### Requires user JWT token
### File upload is REQUIRED for attachments
### The authenticated user's ID is automatically used

### STEP 1: Get Upload URL for Attachment File
POST {{baseUrl}}/s3/upload-url
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fileName": "portfolio-sample.pdf",
  "fileType": "document",
  "filePurpose": "tag"
}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "data": {
###     "uploadUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###     "file": {
###       "id": "file-uuid-here",
###       "fileName": "portfolio-sample.pdf",
###       "fileType": "document",
###       "filePurpose": "tag",
###       "url": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###       ...
###     },
###     "uploadToken": "token-string-here"
###   }
### }

### STEP 2: Upload File to S3
### Use the uploadUrl from Step 1 to upload the actual file
### Note: Replace {{uploadUrl}} with the actual URL from Step 1 response

PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./path/to/your/portfolio-sample.pdf

### STEP 3: Create Tag Attachment
### After uploading file to S3, use the fileId, uploadToken, and purpose from Step 1
### IMPORTANT: fileUrl must be an array, even for single files
### The userId is automatically set from the authenticated user

POST {{baseUrl}}/tags/{{tagId}}/attachments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fileUrl": [
    {
      "fileId": "file-uuid-from-step-1",
      "token": "token-from-step-1",
      "purpose": "tag"
    }
  ]
}

### Example with actual UUID:
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000/attachments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fileUrl": [
    {
      "fileId": "file-uuid-here",
      "token": "token-here",
      "purpose": "tag"
    }
  ]
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Attachment created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "attachment-uuid",
###     "tagId": "tag-uuid",
###     "userId": "user-uuid",
###     "fileUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###     "status": "pending",
###     "rejectionReason": null,
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 5. LIST ALL ATTACHMENTS
### ============================================
### Get all tag attachments with optional filters
### No authentication required
### Supports query parameters: status, tagId, userId

### List All Attachments (No Filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### List Attachments by Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments?status=pending
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### List Attachments by Tag
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments?tagId={{tagId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### List Attachments by User
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments?userId={{userId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### List Attachments with Multiple Filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments?status=accepted&tagId={{tagId}}&userId={{userId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Query Parameters:
### - status: Filter by status - "pending", "accepted", or "rejected" (optional)
### - tagId: Filter by tag UUID (optional)
### - userId: Filter by user UUID (optional)

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Attachments fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "attachment-uuid",
###       "tagId": "tag-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "fileUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###       "status": "pending",
###       "rejectionReason": null,
###       "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### 6. GET USER TAGS WITH ATTACHMENTS
### ============================================
### Get all tags for a specific user with their attachments
### No authentication required
### Returns tags grouped with their attachments

GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/user/{{userId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example with actual UUID:
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/user/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "User tags with attachments fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "tag": {
###         "id": "tag-uuid",
###         "name": "Web Development",
###         "badgeUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###         "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###         "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###       },
###       "attachments": [
###         {
###           "id": "attachment-uuid",
###           "tagId": "tag-uuid",
###           "userId": "user-uuid",
###           "fileUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###           "status": "accepted",
###           "rejectionReason": null,
###           "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###           "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###         }
###       ]
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### 7. UPDATE ATTACHMENT STATUS
### ============================================
### Update the status of a tag attachment (accept/reject/pending)
### Requires user JWT token
### Status can be: "pending", "accepted", or "rejected"
### If status is "rejected", rejectionReason is REQUIRED

### Accept Attachment
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "accepted"
}

### Example with actual UUID:
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "accepted"
}

### Reject Attachment (rejectionReason is required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "rejected",
  "rejectionReason": "The portfolio does not meet our quality standards. Please submit higher resolution samples."
}

### Set Status to Pending
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "pending"
}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Attachment status updated successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "attachment-uuid",
###     "tagId": "tag-uuid",
###     "userId": "user-uuid",
###     "fileUrl": "https://ajwadi.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/tag/...",
###     "status": "accepted",
###     "rejectionReason": null,
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:05:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### Error Response (Missing Rejection Reason):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Validation error",
###   "errors": [
###     {
###       "field": "rejectionReason",
###       "message": "rejectionReason is required when status is rejected"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Endpoints requiring authentication:
###      * POST /api/tags (create tag)
###      * POST /api/tags/:tagId/attachments (create attachment)
###      * PATCH /api/tags/attachments/:id/status (update status)
###    - Endpoints without authentication:
###      * GET /api/tags (list all tags)
###      * GET /api/tags/attachments (list attachments)
###      * GET /api/tags/user/:userId (get user tags)

### 2. FILE UPLOAD FLOW
###    - Step 1: Get upload URL from /api/s3/upload-url
###    - Step 2: Upload file to S3 using the signed URL (PUT request)
###    - Step 3: Use fileId, token, and purpose in the API request
###    - File upload tokens are required for security and validation
###    - Purpose must match: "tag" for tag badges and attachments

### 3. VALIDATION RULES
###    - Tag name: Required, 1-100 characters
###    - Badge URL: Optional, can be file upload token object or string
###    - Attachment file URL: Required, must be file upload token object
###    - Attachment status: Required, must be "pending", "accepted", or "rejected"
###    - Rejection reason: Required when status is "rejected", max 500 characters

### 4. ATTACHMENT STATUSES
###    - pending: Initial status when attachment is created
###    - accepted: Attachment has been approved
###    - rejected: Attachment has been rejected (requires rejectionReason)

### 5. ERROR RESPONSES
###    - 400 Bad Request: Validation errors (missing fields, invalid format, etc.)
###    - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid authentication token
###    - 404 Not Found: Tag, attachment, or user not found
###    - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

### 6. FILE UPLOAD TOKEN FORMAT
###    When uploading files, use this format in the request body:
###    {
###      "fileUrl": [
###        {
###          "fileId": "uuid-from-s3-upload-url-response",
###          "token": "token-from-s3-upload-url-response",
###          "purpose": "tag"
###        }
###      ]
###    }
###    Note: Even for single files, it must be an array

### 7. USAGE EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Create Tag Without Badge
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Mobile Development"
}

### Example 2: Create Tag With Badge
### (After uploading badge file to S3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "UI/UX Design",
  "badgeUrl": [
    {
      "fileId": "badge-file-uuid",
      "token": "badge-upload-token",
      "purpose": "tag"
    }
  ]
}

### Example 3: Create Attachment
### (After uploading attachment file to S3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags/{{tagId}}/attachments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "fileUrl": [
    {
      "fileId": "attachment-file-uuid",
      "token": "attachment-upload-token",
      "purpose": "tag"
    }
  ]
}

### Example 4: List Pending Attachments for a Tag
GET {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments?status=pending&tagId={{tagId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example 5: Accept Attachment
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "accepted"
}

### Example 6: Reject Attachment
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tags/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "rejected",
  "rejectionReason": "The submitted portfolio does not demonstrate sufficient experience in this area."
}

### 8. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Use descriptive tag names that clearly identify the skill or category
###    - Upload high-quality badge images for better visual representation
###    - When rejecting attachments, provide clear and constructive rejection reasons
###    - Regularly review pending attachments to maintain system quality
###    - Use query filters when listing attachments to improve performance

### 9. SECURITY NOTES
###    - File upload tokens are required to prevent unauthorized file associations
###    - Tokens have expiration times for security
###    - Users can only create attachments for themselves (userId is set from token)
###    - Status updates require authentication

### 10. INTEGRATION NOTES
###     - Tags are used to categorize users and their skills
###     - Attachments allow users to provide proof of their skills
###     - Attachment status workflow: pending → accepted/rejected
###     - Tags can exist without badges, but attachments require files
###     - User tags with attachments are grouped by tag for easy display
